<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13772" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπό-σπασμα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>,
			τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>that which is torn off, a piece, rag, shred,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phd.</u>
				113b
			</span></i>; <i>branch, division of a tribe,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Str.
				9.5.12
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Agatharch.
				57
			</span></i>: generally, <i>a detached portion</i> or <i>particle,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψυχῆς καὶ σώματος ἀ. τὸ σπέρμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epicur.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					329
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Zeno Stoic.
				1.36
			</span></i>, Chrysipp.ib.<i><span class="en">
				2.191
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.119
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μύθου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Corn.
					<u>ND</u>
					17
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>avulsion, tearing apart</i> of bones, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Off.</u>
				23
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				18(2).887
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
